# Python bytecode caches, anywhere in the tree (scripts/ holds the
# build/audit infrastructure; tests/dotnet_adapter_goldens/ imports it).
__pycache__/
# Unix core dumps ONLY. These MUST be anchored (leading /) and match files, not
# dirs — a bare `core` pattern matches any path component named core at any depth,
# and on a case-insensitive filesystem (macOS) it also swallowed the entire
# src/SignalWire/Core/ SOURCE tree, leaving those .cs files untracked. That built a
# green-but-incomplete SDK on CI's fresh checkout and failed the tests with CS0234
# (SignalWire.Core.Agent "does not exist"). Anchor + trailing-nothing keeps them
# scoped to real core dumps at the repo root.
/core
/core.[0-9]*
# dotnet-script tool provisioned by the SWAIG-CLI gate (scripts/run-ci.sh)
.dotnet-tools/

# sw-verify repo-local scratch
.sw-tmp/
